https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RjiBgK1s7Q8  (Capo 1)

There's also a version in G which may be easier to play as it avoids the (Bb) but to play with the recording you have to capo at the 6th fret.

TIP:  If transposing, play the root chord of the transposed (CaddG) and (Gadd) and add the 5th note as necessary.

TIP:  I normally avoid the (Bb) like Ebola but for some reason I find it playable here.  Maybe because this is my favorite Emmylou song and I'm trying extra hard.

TIP:  You can play this song without the (CaddG) but it helps accentuate Emmylou's aching high notes. 
     

